application  choupoSolve;

//  AUDIENCE.  A SHOWCASE composes engineering (bin/curate/check_case_tiers):
//  a drug-product plant -- wet granulation with a fluid-bed dryer, tableting,
//  an aqueous film coat dried by hot air, a batch plan, quoted equipment, a
//  GMP building -- is not one feature being isolated, it is the base case a
//  pharmaceutical project group starts from (DEV.md 4c C104, C110).
tier         showcase;
description  "DONEPEZIL HYDROCHLORIDE 10 mg AND 5 mg FILM-COATED TABLETS, TWO PRODUCTS in campaigns on one drug-product plant (the API is BOUGHT): WET GRANULATION -- the API, lactose monohydrate, maize starch and microcrystalline cellulose wetted in a high-shear granulator with an aqueous hydroxypropyl-cellulose binder solution and dried in a fluid bed (`solidDryer`, hot air, the starch's sorption isotherm) -- milling, a final blend with magnesium stearate, tableting with rejects, an aqueous hypromellose film coat dried off by hot air, and packaging. The excipients are the reference product's (ARICEPT SmPC section 6.1) and the 174.33 mg of lactose per 10 mg tablet is its section 2; every other quantity is an author-set assumption. The steady flowsheet is the material balance per unit of product (720 000 tablets/h pressed, the fluid bed's own drying rate, is a basis); a MULTIPRODUCT BATCH PLAN (system/postDict) sizes each step for a 300 kg lot of either strength, counts the lots a year for 90 million 10 mg and 60 million 5 mg tablets, runs them in single-product campaigns in a declared order with a direction-dependent clean between them (colour carry-over: white after yellow is the long one), and finds the pace of the granulation and tableting trains. Blending, granulation, milling, tableting and packaging are MASS-BALANCE PLACEHOLDERS (no equipment physics). No organic solvent, no spray drying, no hazardous area. The 5 mg tablet is the 10 mg tablet at half the weight (the same blend), so the one steady balance serves both.";
verbosity    2;

reports
{
    streamTable   {}
    massBalance   {}
    energyBalance {}
    computed      {}
    spreadsheet   {}
}

